COMMENT                                                                         SURVEY  = 'FIRST   '                                                            COMMENT ****************************************************************        COMMENT Properties of the original survey data follow:                          COMMENT Provenance: The FIRST project team-                                     COMMENT R.J. Becker, D.H. Helfand, R.L. White and M.D. Gregg.                   COMMENT Copyright:  1994, University of California (see below)                  COMMENT Regime:     Radio                                                       COMMENT Number of surveys: 1                                                    COMMENT Frequency:  1.4 GHz Continuum                                           COMMENT Coverage:   Eventually will cover entire North Galactic                 COMMENT Polar region (about 10,000 square degrees).                             COMMENT Pixel Scale: 1.8"/pixel                                                 COMMENT Pixel Units: Janskies/beam                                              COMMENT Resolution:  5"                                                         COMMENT Coordinate system:  Equatorial                                          COMMENT Equinox:     2000                                                       COMMENT Projection:  Orthographic                                               COMMENT Epoch:       1994-1997                                                  COMMENT Reference:   FIRST Home page -- https://sundog.stsci.edu/top.html       COMMENT ****************************************************************        COMMENT                                                                         TELESCOP= 'VLA     '                                                            BUNIT   = 'JY/BEAM '                                                            HISTORY The FIRST VLA Survey: Copyright 1994 University of California           HISTORY Permission is granted for publication and reproduction of this          HISTORY material for scholarly, educational, and private non-commercial         HISTORY use.  Inquiries for potential commercial uses should be                 HISTORY addressed to:                                                           HISTORY Robert Becker                                                           HISTORY Physics Dept                                                            HISTORY University of California                                                HISTORY Davis, CA  95616                                                        HISTORY -----------------------------------------------------------             HISTORY The VLA FIRST Survey                                                    HISTORY R.H. Becker            R.L. White         D.J. Helfand                  HISTORY UC Davis and IGPP, LLNL       STScI         Columbia University         HISTORY The FIRST survey (Faint Images of the Radio Sky at Twenty-cm) is a      HISTORY high angular resolution survey of the North Galactic Cap intended to    HISTORY match the 10,000 deg**2 survey area of the Sloan Digital Sky Survey     HISTORY (Gunn and Knapp 1992 PASP 43, 267).  Observations are made in the       HISTORY VLA's B configuration operating at frequencies of 1365 and 1435 MHz in  HISTORY the bandwidth synthesis mode. The synthesized beam has a FWHM of 5.4".  HISTORY Each field is observed for 3 minutes, resulting in a typical image rms  HISTORY of <0.15 mJy/beam.  The raw UV data from the observations are archived  HISTORY at the VLA and are available on the day they are taken without the      HISTORY standard proprietary period.  The fully self-calibrated UV datasets     HISTORY for each pointing are also archived at the NRAO.                        HISTORY Source positions derived from FIRST images have an error of 0.5" rms    HISTORY for the weakest discernible point sources (~0.75 mJy) and               HISTORY substantially smaller uncertainties for brighter sources. The source    HISTORY surface density is ~100 per square degree. The grid of images on the    HISTORY sky is sufficiently dense that considerable improvement in sensitivity  HISTORY can be obtained by coadding adjacent fields.  These coadded images, of  HISTORY which this is an example, comprise one of the principal data products   HISTORY of the FIRST Survey. The maps are labelled as HHMMM+-DDMMM (with        HISTORY implied decimal points before the final M's) corresponding to the       HISTORY J2000 coordinates of the field center to the nearest 6"; e.g., the      HISTORY field centered at 07 42 00 +30 45 36 is labelled 07420+30456. The       HISTORY images are stored as binary FITS image files with appropriate           HISTORY extensions; the images have 1.8" x 1.8" pixels, and vary in size        HISTORY depending on declination.  Each image has an associated NN table which  HISTORY lists all the possible fields which could contribute to the image and   HISTORY indicates which were available at the time this version of the image    HISTORY was created.                                                            HISTORY Details of the survey design, pipeline processing algorithms, and       HISTORY catalog generation may be found in Becker et al. 1995; this paper,      HISTORY along with further information on FIRST, is retrievable via the FIRST   HISTORY WWW home-page: https://sundog.stsci.edu/ . Users interested in deriving HISTORY quantitative information from the maps for scientific purposes are      HISTORY advised to read the FIRST paper first.  Questions or comments on the    HISTORY FIRST survey should be addressed to Bob Becker at bob@igpp.llnl.gov or  HISTORY 510-423-0664.                                                           HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY Settings used in processing:                                            